This is a fork, not a vendored copy. crossglyph adds fourteen knobs upstream does
not have: gamma, AA thresholds, weight, slant, hinting, grayscale hinting, mono
rasterizing, stem darkening, line height, letter and word spacing, kerning as a
factor, ligatures and proportional figures. It also rasterizes a variable font
at a chosen instance, where upstream takes the file's default.
`uv run tools/refresh_cpfont.py` fetches upstream and shows a diff against the
fork so changes can be merged by hand. Do not overwrite.

The bundled Noto fallback faces are NOT forked -- they are still read
from the crosspoint-tools clone beside this one, since only the script diverges.
